From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 15 Jul 2026 13:40:18 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 07190/11362] [outer-loop] REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-9: non-hidden-state
 game -- different gate, documented lever doesn't clear it

Answers REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-8's follow-up: test a game NOT in
HIDDEN_STATE_GAME_IDS, where that specific trust gate doesn't apply.

Added sp80 (same registry L1->L2 shallow-frontier framing as
sk48/cd82) to GAMES -- confirmed not a HIDDEN_STATE_GAME_IDS member.

Correctness fix found first: running sp80 alone silently overwrote
the committed g50t/sk48/cd82 outer_loop_sge_smoke_test_suite.json
with a 1-game summary (restored via git checkout, uncommitted at the
time). Fixed: a subset run (explicit game args) now always writes to
a game-suffixed summary path, never colliding with the full-suite
default.

Ran sp80 three ways. Baseline: real_max_level_observed=0, consistent
with the other 3 games. --induction: still 0, skipped with
"world_model_accuracy_below_threshold" -- a DIFFERENT reason than
REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-8's hidden-state finding, confirming sp80 takes the
other code branch (WorldModelVerifier(...).score(engine) < 0.5).
That branch's own source comment names CARNOT_ARC_TRUST_METRIC=
cell_recall as "the coordinated-redesign lever for the 0.08 wall."
Tried it: still skipped, still 0 -- verify_cell_recall was genuinely
0.0 too, not just verify_accuracy under the stricter default metric.
The documented lever exists to rescue an imperfect-but-useful model
a strict metric unfairly zeroes; sp80's candidate scores zero on the
lenient metric as well, so switching doesn't help here.

Net effect across all 4 games tested: induction has never reached
the actual LLM call, for two structurally similar reasons (a cheap
non-LLM candidate is trust-checked before the expensive call, and
none of the 4 candidates clear their bar with only ~25 cold-start
transitions). Consistent with, not new evidence against, the still-
open REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-7 follow-up: whether a much larger budget lets
these pre-checks pass at all.

3 new tests (subset-run summary path fix, spec-declaration). Spec:
REQ-ARC-FCP-5699-9 with its own scenario.

